course: dictionary
lesson: 14185
title: Montage: many clips in one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A montage is a quick series of short clips or pictures, put together to show lots of things happening, or time passing. «The film showed a training montage: Sam ran, lifted weights and kicked a ball, all in one minute.» The word "all in one minute" is a clue that a lot happened very quickly.
explain: Montage is also used in art and school projects. «For our project, we made a photo montage of our summer holiday.» Here a montage is one picture made from many photos put together. The clue is the word "photo" and the idea of many things joined as one.
explain: When you meet montage, ask yourself: is a lot happening quickly, or is time passing? Look for clue words like "quickly", "many", "a series of" and "all in one". If your meaning still fits the sentence, you have probably understood it.
fact: A montage is a quick series of short clips or pictures put together.
fact: In films and TV, a montage often shows time passing or many things happening.
fact: A photo montage is one picture made from many photos or pieces.
fact: «Training montage» and «photo montage» are common phrases; «a montage of» means a collection of things shown together.
fact: Look at the words around montage, such as "quickly" or "many", to help you understand it.
exercise: «The film showed a training montage: Sam ran, lifted weights and kicked a ball, all in one minute.» What is a montage here? | *A quick series of short clips showing lots happening | A long, slow scene with one character talking | A set of photos of the cast | A list of the actors' names at the end
exercise: In art class, Priya made a photo montage of her favourite places. What is a photo montage? | *Many photos joined together to make one picture | A map of the school | One large photo taken on a sunny day | A painting of a single tree
exercise: Which clue in a sentence tells you a montage shows time passing? | Words like "sat quietly for hours" | Words like "the teacher said" | *Words like "quickly" or "all in one minute"
test: «The montage showed the seasons changing, from snow to sunshine in just a minute.» What does the montage show? | *Seasons changing quickly, with time passing | Only one season, all year round | A tiny insect crawling on a leaf | A list of rules for the seasons
test: Which phrase means many photos put together into one picture? | a training montage | a sunny day at the beach | *a photo montage | a long walk in the park
exam: Which best describes a montage? | A single long shot with no cuts | A type of small dog | *A quick series of short clips or pictures put together | A word meaning very old
